every week on Google cloud labs we  discuss a different lab and go over what  you would learn when you take a lab but  what is quick labs and how can it be  helpful for you a quick lab is an online  learning environment along with a set of  instructions to walk you through a live  real-world and scenario based use case  without needing an account on GCP in a  lab you will have access to the actual  environment you want to learn about not  a simulation or demo environment you can  access the lab environment from anywhere  on the internet using a standard browser  so how do you take a lab first get  started by either creating an account or  signing in find labs by browsing the  quick labs quest or clicking on the lab  catalog and then the laptop the laptop  lets you scroll through all the  available labs read more about a lab by  clicking on the lab of your choice  the lab page opens to the lab manual  page the timer located next to the start  lab button shows the total time that  resources will be made available to take  the lab the lab will end after the timer  finishes counting down to begin a lab  click the start lab button the lab will  not start until you have selected the  start lab button and enter the  appropriate credits or token code the  cost of the lab is indicated in credits  some labs are free and require no  credits each dollar spent buys one  credit labs vary in number of credits  required when you are finished with the  lab click the end lab button and leave a  review  you notice something else in quick labs  and that is quests quick lap quests are  introductory in advanced learning paths  that consist of collection of labs  organized by technologies specific cloud  services and practical use cases  completion of the required labs that are  part of quick labs quest will earn you  badges that recognize your hands-on  experience your quick labs quest badges  will be permanent part of your quick  labs account and profile referencing  your accomplishments can be a positive  mark of distinction you're encouraged to  share your achievements on social media  for example you could do this by adding  a link on your LinkedIn profile pointing  to your badge  there are many labs on quick labs let us  know in comments below which one you're  taking and how it went  thank you for watching and whenever  you're ready to sign up we're giving you  a $300 credit for GCP just click on the  link in the description below  [Music]
 

